\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Mexico central bankers flag peso risk, some see pre-Fed hike\b0\par\par\uc2 331 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Mai 2016\par 17:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Recasts with possible move before Fed, adds \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  comments)\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY, May 19 (Reuters) - \uc2 Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board is worried global financial volatility could spur a deeper slump in the peso, and some of its members think it might need to hike interest rates before the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2 , according to the minutes of their last policy meeting.\par \par \uc2 Policymakers voted 5 to 0 to keep their benchmark rate at 3.75 percent at their May 5 meeting, according to the minutes released on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had surprised markets with a 50 basis point hike in February.\par \par \uc2 According to the minutes of the last meeting, some board members thought Mexico may need to raise interest rates again independently of any move by the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  to tighten borrowing costs due to the risks to inflation.\par \par \uc2 The peso has weakened sharply since late 2014, but inflation so far has been surprisingly cool.\par \par \uc2 One member thought there was enough slack in the economy to raise rates without hitting growth.\par \par \uc2 Most members thought that annual inflation would end the year around its 3 percent target, but the majority worried about the risk that global volatility could spark a "disorderly" drop in the peso that could have a bigger impact on inflation.\par \par \uc2 A sharp drop in the peso during February pushed \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to directly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets for the first time since 2009 and to unexpectedly raise interest rates after an unannounced meeting.\par \par \uc2 Since the bank's policy announcement early this month, the peso tumbled again, hitting a fresh three-month low on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The speed of the peso's recent tumble has sparked speculation the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could soon \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to try and cushion the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fall with direct dollar sales.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Michael O'Boyle and Gabriel Stargardter Editing by W Simon) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-5-19T16:15:41.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160519ec5j01fpe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
