\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Mexico \highlight\uc2  peso hits 3-month low, market expects more  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 459 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Mai 2016\par 19:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 MEXICO\b0 \highlight\uc2  CITY, May 18 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso slumped to a three-month low on Wednesday, with the speed of its recent tumble sparking speculation the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could soon \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to try and cushion the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fall.\par \par \uc2 The peso sank as much as 0.9 percent to 18.4510 per dollar, its weakest since February. The peso has lost nearly 7 percent this month, making it the second worst performer among the world's 36 most-traded \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , behind the South African rand.\par \par \uc2 A prominent group of Mexican economists on Tuesday said the peso was under a speculative attack, and analysts said the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could soon sell dollars directly to the market, as it did in February.\par \par \uc2 "They are willing to use their firepower," said Alberto Ramos, an economist at Goldman Sachs in New York.\par \par \uc2 "You need to anchor the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at some point, if the peso goes to 19 or 20 (to the dollar) that could change the inflation outlook and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is very mindful of that," Ramos said.\par \par \uc2 By midday Wednesday, the peso had pared losses to trade 0.45 percent lower at 18.3625.\par \par \uc2 A sharp peso drop in February pushed \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to directly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets for the first time since 2009 and to unexpectedly raise interest rates after an unannounced meeting.\par \par \uc2 Then, Mexican policymakers said the peso was being targeted by electronic trading programs and that its losses did not match with the relatively sound position of the economy.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, Deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Javier Guzman said the bank may need to raise interest rates if global events hit the peso enough to affect inflation expectations. So far, inflation has been slower than expected.\par \par \uc2 Emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been slammed by renewed expectations the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  could tighten borrowing costs, which could sap demand for higher-yielding but riskier assets.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso is one of world's most liquid \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and unlike many other emerging markets there are no capital controls on its trade. That makes it easier to bet against the peso when global sentiment on risky assets turns sour.\par \par \uc2 "It's a cheap proxy for expressing a negative view on emerging markets," said \uc2 UBS\uc2  strategist Manik Narain.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso bonds are among the most widely held debt among those issued in emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Foreign investors hold over 2 trillion pesos ($109 billion) in peso debt, and many need to hedge their positions when the peso slumps, further driving volatility, Narain said.\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 18.3800 Mexican pesos) (Additional reporting by Sujata Rao-Coverley in London Editing by W Simon) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-5-18T18:05:49.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160518ec5i01jv5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal25