\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil real hits 8-month high as Latam  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  rally\b0\par\par\uc2 534 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 April 2016\par 01:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SAO PAULO, April 29 (Reuters) - Brazil's real surged to an\par eight-month high on Friday, prompting the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par to step up \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to derail the rally, while Colombia and\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Mexico\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's pesos also hit their strongest levels this year.\par     Dovish signs from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  have fueled\par strong gains in Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  this week.\par     The dollar index, a measure of the greenback's value\par against a basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , was on course for its third\par consecutive monthly decline for the first time in five years. \par     Investors have pared their bets on multiple interest rate\par hikes this year after the U.S. economy nearly ground to a halt\par in the first quarter. This helped to drive demand for\par higher-yielding emerging market assets.  \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Brazil's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , in its first \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in a week,\par offered up to $2.5 billion in reverse \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swaps in three\par auctions after the real hit 3.45 per dollar.\par     Other Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also strengthened. The\par Mexican peso rose more than 0.5 percent to a four-month\par high on stronger-than-expected first-quarter preliminary GDP\par data for the region's No. 2 economy. \par     "The dollar trend remains bearish. The (Brazilian) \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  came in and it continued to fall (against the real)\par anyway," said Glauber Romano, trader at brokerage Intercam.\par     Colombia's peso jumped nearly 1 percent to close at\par its strongest since early November. \par     After the market close, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Colombia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  unexpectedly\par increased its benchmark interest rate by half a percentage point\par to stem rising inflation. \par     Latam stock markets were also firmer, with the broader MSCI\par Latin American stock index up 0.4 percent, as\par commodities prices gained.\par     Shares of Mexican media group Televisa SAB \par jumped more than 8 percent after the company reported solid\par sales growth despite a 59-percent drop in first-quarter profit.\par     A sharp drop in shares of planemaker \f28 \uc2 \f2 Embraer SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par capped gains in Brazilian stocks. Shares of the world's\par third-largest commercial jet maker fell nearly 4 percent after a\par decline in profit margins in the first quarter. \par \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 2115 GMT:\par         \par  Stock indexes                               daily %    YTD %\par                                               change   change\par                                   Latest              \par  MSCI Emerging Markets               840.19    -0.46      5.8\par  MSCI LatAm                         2292.06     0.36    25.26\par  Brazil Bovespa                    53910.51    -0.74    24.36\par  Mexico IPC                        45784.77     0.56     6.53\par  Chile IPSA                         4002.07    -0.51     8.75\par  Chile IGPA                        19655.14    -0.42     8.28\par  Argentina MerVal                  13724.07    -0.11    17.55\par  Colombia IGBC                      9961.63     -1.2    16.55\par  Venezuela IBC                     15670.96      0.1     7.42\par                                                              \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                                   daily %    YTD %\par                                               change   change\par                                      Latest           \par  Brazil real                         3.4382     1.68    14.80\par  Mexico peso                          17.17     0.54     0.35\par                                                       \par  Chile peso                             660     0.08     7.53\par  Colombia peso                      2846.05     0.98    11.36\par  Peru sol                             3.287    -0.33     3.86\par  Argentina peso (interbank)         14.2500     0.70    -8.89\par                                                       \par  Argentina peso (parallel)            14.61     0.68    -2.33\par                                                       \par                                                              \par  \par  (Reporting by Flavia Bohone; Writing by Silvio Cascione;\par Editing by Richard Chang)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-4-30T00:03:02.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160429ec4t023ul\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
