\par\par \b \uc2 Mexican Stocks End Lower, Peso Weakens Against U.S. Dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 306 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2016\par 21:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY--Mexican stocks closed lower Tuesday, while the peso weakened against the dollar, as falling oil prices and uncertainty about the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2 's forthcoming policy decision dominated sentiment among investors.\par \par \uc2 The IPC index of leading issues closed down 1.1% at 44210 points, on volume of 200 million shares valued at 6.2 billion pesos ($347 million).\par \par \uc2 Cement maker \uc2 Cemex\uc2  closed down 2.2% at 10.67 pesos, while Mexican miner Penoles fell 3.7% to 219.34 pesos. Telecom firm \uc2 America Movil\uc2  fell 2.7% to 12.96 pesos.\par \par \uc2 The price of oil remained the focus for investors. Brent crude fell almost 2% at $38.77 a barrel. The price of U.S. crude oil also fell.\par \par \uc2 Mexico is the world's ninth-largest oil producer and exports around 1.2 million barrels of oil a day. About 20% of the federal budget comes from oil revenue.\par \par \uc2 The peso lost some ground against the dollar. The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed in Mexico City at 17.8880 pesos, according to Infosel, compared with 17.7580 pesos at the close on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Since mid-February, when Mexican authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the peso has gained 6.9% against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the exchange commission announced on Feb. 17 a surprise interest rate increase of 50 basis points, as well as budget cuts and discretionary \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange markets.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to keep interest rates unchanged at 3.75% after February's surprise rate increase, given that inflation remains low and the exchange market has calmed down in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 Write to Juan Montes at juan.montes@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 March 15, 2016 16:17 ET (20:17 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160315ec3f0040i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
