\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Colombia, Mexico pesos fall after last-minute oil price drop\b0\par\par\uc2 503 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Februar 2016\par 02:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Updates with closing prices)\par \par \uc2 By Bruno Federowski\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Feb 26 (Reuters) - Both the Mexican and Colombian pesos dropped on Friday, hurt by fresh U.S. data that boosted the dollar and a slump in the oil price late in the session.\par \par \uc2 The two \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which have hit a series of record lows, had been on track to post weekly gains for a second time in a row, but in the end only the Colombian peso posted a gain for the week.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso ended the day down 0.88 percent at 18.289 pesos per dollar, and was down 0.35 percent for the week. The Colombian peso lost 0.95 percent on Friday, but rose 0.32 percent over the last seven days.\par \par \uc2 The late fade in oil prices prompted players to take profits on winning positions in the wake of an early rally that pushed benchmark Brent crude prices to their highest level since early January.\par \par \uc2 A stronger-than-expected revision of U.S. fourth-quarter economic growth boosted the dollar index, a measure of the greenback's value against six major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The index gained 0.8 percent to post its best weekly performance since November.\par \par \uc2 Despite Friday's losses, the Mexican and Colombian pesos have shown recent signs of recovery as rebounding oil prices, talk of stimulus measures in China and stronger U.S. growth extended the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' bounce from recent all-time lows.\par \par \uc2 The rally was also triggered by stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies announced last week to curb inflation expectations.\par \par \uc2 "The measures were timely and forceful, as well as necessary to add two-way risk back into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," wrote \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  analysts in a client note about \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The bank only used up $2 billion in dollar sales and seemed to be successful in supporting the peso, they added.\par \par \uc2 Fitch Ratings\uc2  affirmed Mexico's BBB-plus ratings on Friday, and affirmed a stable outlook, citing the country's diversified economic base and track record of disciplined fiscal policies.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Colombia did not even need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. Although the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reduced the threshold triggering automatic dollar call option sales, the bank has not held any auctions so far.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real underperformed, weakening over 1 percent against the dollar, as it suffered from portfolio rebalancing trades usually conducted at the end of the month. Traders often try to influence a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate calculated by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the last session of the month, which is used to settle futures contracts, boosting volatility.\par \par \uc2 Brazil stocks fell for a fourth straight session, pressured by a slump in shares of \uc2 BRF SA\uc2 . The food processor announced several management changes after posting higher-than-expected profits in the fourth quarter. (Reporting by Bruno Federowski; additional reporting by Paula Arend Laier, Editing by G Crosse and Leslie Adler) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-2-27T02:04:54.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160227ec2r001jl\par }\page {\par\fs20