\par\par \b \uc2 Mexico Stocks Close Lower; Peso Weakens on Oil's Drop\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Harrup   \par \uc2 339 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Februar 2016\par 22:40\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY -- Mexican stocks closed lower Tuesday, and the peso weakened against the U.S. dollar after Saudi Arabia said it wouldn't cut oil production to shore up prices, sending crude prices lower.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark IPC stock index closed down 0.8% at 43,217 points on volume of 185.7 million shares worth 5.55 billion pesos ($305 million).\par \par \uc2 Telecoms company \uc2 America Movil\uc2  shares fell 0.6% to MXN12.00, and cement maker \uc2 Cemex\uc2  shares closed down 1.2% at MXN9.68.\par \par \uc2 Bottler Coca-Cola Femsa shares slipped 0.5% to MXN131.00. The company reported a 6% rise in fourth-quarter net earnings per share, as sales increased 10% due largely to higher prices. Operating profit rose 9.2%.\par \par \uc2 The peso weakened against the U.S. dollar as oil prices fell after the Saudi oil minister, Ali al-Naimi, dashed hopes for agreements among producers to cut production. The peso was quoted in Mexico City at MXN18.1990 to the dollar, according to Infosel, compared with MXN18.0660 late Monday,.\par \par \uc2 Banco Base said the speculative effect on the peso was limited by the possibility of the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the market.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  commission last week suspended the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's scheduled dollar auctions and replaced them with the possibility of direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reported that it sold $2 billion last week under the new \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  method.\par \par \uc2 "Although rule-based USD selling auctions have the benefits of transparency, they tend to be used by speculators to profit from the liquidity provisioned by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," \uc2 Barclays\uc2  said in a report. "In the current setting, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  not only has the discretion to provide liquidity to the market when it considers it necessary, but will effectively be able to partially curb speculative behavior."\par \par \uc2 Write to Anthony Harrup at anthony.harrup@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 February 23, 2016 16:40 ET (21:40 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160223ec2n004mq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
