\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Mexico \highlight\uc2 's Stocks End Lower, Peso Strengthens After  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 279 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Februar 2016\par 22:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 MEXICO\b0 \highlight\uc2  CITY--Mexican stocks ended lower Friday, while the peso strengthened for a third consecutive session after this week's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The IPC index of leading issues closed down 0.3% at 43,376 points on volume of 182 million shares valued at 5.5 billion pesos ($302 million).\par \par \uc2 Telecommunications company \uc2 America Movil\uc2  shares fell 2.5% to 11.93 pesos, and cement maker \uc2 Cemex\uc2  shares closed up 0.5% at 9.26 pesos. Bread maker Bimbo closed up 1.6% to 52.83 pesos.\par \par \uc2 Uncertainty over U.S. monetary policy and global growth prospects, and falling oil prices hit stocks.\par \par \uc2 But the Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gained more ground against the greenback, a sign that the measures announced Wednesday by Mexican authorities to support the peso -- including a surprise 50 basis-point rate increase to 3.75% and discretionary \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets -- are paying off, at least for now.\par \par \uc2 The peso was quoted in Mexico City at 18.2150 to the dollar, according to Infosel, compared with 18.2965 late Thursday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a record low in early February, when it weakened to more than 19 pesos to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly early Wednesday, selling dollars without previous notice -- the first discretionary \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  into the market since the 2009 crisis.\par \par \uc2 Higher interest rates in Mexico make the peso more attractive for investors seeking higher-yielding alternatives, given still very low rates in the U.S.\par \par \uc2 Write to Juan Montes at juan.montes@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 February 19, 2016 16:36 ET (21:36 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160219ec2j003rj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
