\par\par \b \uc2 Mexico Fires on All Cylinders to Support the Peso\b0\par\par\uc2 By Amy Guthrie   \par \uc2 437 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Februar 2016\par 22:50\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY--The Mexican peso strengthened Wednesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  unleashed new tools in its arsenal to combat the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's free fall.\par \par \uc2 The peso finished around 18.3660 pesos to the U.S. dollar compared with 18.8920 pesos Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bank of Mexico\uc2  unexpectedly raised its overnight lending rate target by a half percentage point, to 3.75%, after an unscheduled meeting. At the same time, the bank scrapped its preset U.S. dollar auctions, which critics say were burning through reserves while doing little to support the peso.\par \par \uc2 Instead, \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will take the unusual step of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market without notice. \uc2 Bank of Mexico\uc2  Gov. Agustin Carstens said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  made discretionary dollar sales early Wednesday as a "protest" against the level to which the market had pushed the exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 The peso--the world's eighth-most-traded \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with an estimated $135 billion a day traded in the dollar-peso market--is often used to hedge exposure to other emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , making it vulnerable to the changing moods of global markets.\par \par \uc2 The peso weakened 14% against the dollar in 2015 and has fallen an additional 6% this year, largely due to the tumble in oil prices. Earlier this month, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reached a record-low of about 19.4500 pesos to the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 "We do not know if these policies will successfully stabilize the exchange rate, but we believe it is as aggressive it can get," \uc2 Nomura Securities\uc2  wrote.\par \par \uc2 As a preventive measure, the government said it would also reduce spending this year by 132.3 billion pesos ($7.21 billion), or 0.7% of gross domestic product. Of the total, 100 billion pesos would be cut by state oil company \uc2 Petroleos Mexicanos\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, more rate increases could be in order, which analysts caution could become a drag on economic growth.\par \par \uc2 "If volatility continues and \b \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  fail to stabilize the MXN, higher hikes might be implemented, which should definitely affect growth with no clear effect in local financial markets," \uc2 Barclays\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 In equities, the IPC index of Mexico's most-traded shares rose 1.1% to 43585 points on Wednesday. Blue-chip cement maker \uc2 Cemex\uc2  stoked the gains, rising 8.9% to 9.57 pesos, while retailer Walmex slumped 5.1% to 42.40 pesos after disappointing earnings.\par \par \uc2 Write to Amy Guthrie at amy.guthrie@wsj.com<mailto:amy.guthrie@wsj.com>\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 February 17, 2016 16:50 ET (21:50 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160217ec2h004ea\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
