\par\par \b \uc2 Mexico's  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Swing Shows Why  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Matters to ETF Investors -- Barron's Blog\b0\par\par\uc2 By Chris Dieterich   \par \uc2 311 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Februar 2016\par 20:07\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Emerging-market ETF investors are getting a lift from \uc2 Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which surprised markets with efforts to buttress the country's floundering \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Wednesday's move by Banixco reportedly involved selling U.S. dollars to support the Mexican peso, which last week slumped to a record low versus the greenback. Plunging oil prices have wreaked havoc on Mexico's budget, prompting a series of spending cuts. Meanwhile, a weakening peso has imperils borrowers who took on debt in dollar terms by making those debts harder to repay.\par \par \uc2 Sudden \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves carry big-time implications for U.S.-based investors who target overseas markets, a revelation that lured a rush of cash into \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -hedged exchange-traded funds in recent years. \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's surprise \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , like Switzerland's a year ago, means large performance differences for overseas investors based on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  alone.\par \par \uc2 Take note of the market differences for U.S.-based investors in Mexican stocks on Wednesday: Mexico's benchmark IPC stock index rose 0.7% in recent trading, but the \uc2 iShares \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Hedged MSCI Mexico ETF\uc2  ( EWW) rocketed 3.6% higher. That's because the peso shot up more than 3% versus the U.S. dollar. Think of it this way: when you buy a single-country foreign stock ETFs with dollars, you're betting both on stock market performance and on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of a given country.\par \par \uc2 Latin America's second-largest economy gets heavy weight in pan-regional exchange-traded funds. Mexico accounts for more than one-third of exposure in the iShares Latin American ( ILF), which popped 3.2% in recent trading. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  More at Barron's Focus on Funds blog, \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.barrons.com/focusonfunds/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.barrons.com/focusonfunds/}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 February 17, 2016 14:07 ET (19:07 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160217ec2h003ml\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
