\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Mexico's Carstens sees end to dollar auctions with rate hike -paper\b0\par\par\uc2 356 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 2015\par 16:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes from Carstens, background on peso depreciation)\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY, Oct 8 (Reuters) - Mexico aims to dial back its support of the peso when it raises interest rates off their record low, according to an interview with \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor \uc2 Agustin Carstens\uc2  published on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Late last month, Mexico extended its dollar auction program through the end of November to support the peso in the face of global volatility ahead of an expected increase in U.S. borrowing costs.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with Mexican daily El Economista in Lima at meetings of the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  and the \uc2 World Bank\uc2 , Carstens said Mexico did not plan on maintaining its dollar auctions in the medium term.\par \par \uc2 "It's very likely that when interest rates start to rise, (it) will let us reduce the degree of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market," he said. "We will be complementing and at some time substituting this policy for another, using other instruments such as interest rates."\par \par \uc2 Other emerging markets such as Brazil have stepped up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts, but \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  is reluctant to fight the market due to its commitment to a freely floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The peso has hit successive record lows this year and has lost around a quarter of its value against the dollar since last year.\par \par \uc2 Most analysts expect \uc2 Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to raise its main rate off 3.0 percent when the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  hikes, according to a Reuters poll on Sept. 28, but some think the bank could increase rates first if the peso's losses deepen.\par \par \uc2 Minutes from the bank's last policy meeting in September released on Monday showed most of the board see few signs so far that a weak peso has hit inflation, which fell to a fresh record low in September.\par \par \uc2 Carstens told the newspaper that Mexico could adjust its monetary policy if it saw evidence that the peso was fuelling a widespread rise in consumer prices. (Reporting by Michael O'Boyle; Editing by Dave Graham and Meredith Mazzilli)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-10-11T14:47:57.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020151008eba800j4x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
