\par\par \b \uc2 Mexico not targeting any peso-dollar level -finance minister\b0\par\par\uc2 363 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 August 2015\par 20:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY, Aug 22 (Reuters) - Mexico is not targeting a particular peso level against the U.S. dollar, only a liquid market, Finance Minister Luis Videgaray said on Saturday, a day after the Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a fresh low against the greenback.\par \par \uc2 Separately, the minister said the government aimed to send a plan to Congress in the coming days to create special economic areas in parts of the country that have been left behind economically, focusing on Mexico's poorer south.\par \par \uc2 In a speech to lawmakers from the ruling Institutional Revolutionary Party, or PRI, Videgaray said the key objective for policymakers was to ensure that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market conditions did not end up hurting consumers' spending power.\par \par \uc2 Policymakers are watching for signs the peso decline could stoke price pressures, but inflation is tame at the moment, touching a record low of 2.74 percent in July.\par \par \uc2 Still, the peso has fallen by more than 15 percent against the dollar this year, and \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month stepped up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with policymakers saying they could take further steps if necessary.\par \par \uc2 Videgaray said it was crucial to ensure the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market remained "highly liquid", which is why authorities had acted.\par \par \uc2 "Not with the aim of defending a particular Mexican peso level against the dollar. This would be a throwback to another era when the exchange rate was fixed," he said.\par \par \uc2 "Today's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange market are to ensure the liquidity of the market," he continued.\par \par \uc2 It was also crucial the government remained fiscally responsible and upheld \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  autonomy, he said.\par \par \uc2 Congress resumes on Sept. 1, and Videgaray said President Enrique Pena Nieto would soon send lawmakers an initiative to mandate creation of the special economic areas.\par \par \uc2 Such a plan could comprise providing the less-developed zones with fiscal benefits, a special customs regime and a "flexible regulatory framework," Videgaray said. It was also crucial to provide them with better infrastructure, he added.\par \par \uc2 Three southern states of notable importance were Chiapas, Guerrero and Oaxaca, Videgaray said. (Reporting by Dave Graham; Editing by James Dalgleish) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-8-22T19:14:08.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150822eb8m00hlj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
