\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-\uc2 Mexico  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  cuts 2015 growth forecast, signals 'timely' rate move\b0\par\par\uc2 400 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 August 2015\par 00:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  comments on peso, economist comment)               \par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY, Aug 12 (Reuters) - \uc2 Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  revised down its 2015 economic growth outlook on Wednesday, but signaled policymakers would have to adjust interest rates in a "timely" fashion to protect the tumbling peso from further volatility.               \par \par \uc2 In its quarterly inflation report, the bank revised its growth target for this year to between 1.7 and 2.5 percent, from 2 to 3 percent in its last report after weaker-than-expected exports and a slump in domestic oil output.               \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor \uc2 Agustin Carstens\uc2  warned that higher borrowing costs could dampen economic growth, but he said policymakers were ready to raise interest rates "in a timely manner" in order to contain a big slump in the peso.               \par \par \uc2 "What we need to watch is precisely that this exchange rate movement does not have a significant impact on inflation or over the process of price formation," Carstens said.               \par \par \uc2 The peso has been hammered on concerns that an interest rate hike by the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  will drive investors away from emerging markets.               \par \par \uc2 Late last month, \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  commission bolstered its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  programs in an effort to defend the peso and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  warned that it could raise interest rates at any time if needed to keep inflation around its 3 percent target.               \par \par \uc2 Carstens said the stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program had been adequate to brake the peso's depreciation. The peso hit a string of record lows in July but it has traded a bit stronger and has not posted any fresh lows since dollar sales increased.               \par \par \uc2 The bank held steady its growth forecast of 2.5 to 3.5 percent for 2016, saying that a weaker exchange rate would help factories increase exports.               \par \par \uc2 Alexis Milo, an economist at \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  in Mexico, said in a note that the bank's emphasis on growth pared with less concern about the peso slump suggested that policymakers are unlikely to hike before the Fed.               \par \par \uc2 It also said it expects inflation to hold slightly below its 3 percent target for the rest of 2015 and noted limited pressures from the weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on prices.               \par \par \uc2 Mexico's annual inflation rate dropped in July to touch a record-low for a third consecutive month.               \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-8-12T23:57:15.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150812eb8c00r3b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
