\par\par \b \uc2 Mexican Peso Strengthens Further After  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Stocks Rise\b0\par\par\uc2 352 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Juli 2015\par 22:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 MEXICO\b0 \highlight\uc2  CITY--\b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso strengthened Friday for a second consecutive session after authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while stocks rose after a week marked by speculation over when exactly the U.S. Federal Reserve will be rising interest rates.\par \par \uc2 The peso closed in Mexico City at 16.12 against the dollar, according to Infosel, compared with 16.27 at the close Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bounced back from historic lows after Mexico's exchange commission announced Thursday it is increasing the amount of dollars to be sold at auctions to address continued exchange-market volatility. It is now selling $200 million each day, up from $52 million.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, \uc2 Bank of Mexico\uc2 's \uc2 Agustin Carstens\uc2  reinforced the bank's commitment to stem the peso's rout by saying that interest rates could go up "if necessary, at any moment".\par \par \uc2 "If the peso needs higher rates, we can raise rates, independently of what the U.S. Federal Reserve does," said Mr. Carstens in a radio interview. So far, policy makers had ruled out hike rates before the Fed. On Thursday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left the overnight interest rate unchanged at 3%, citing sluggish economic growth and low inflation.\par \par \uc2 Many analysts see the dollar auctions just as a temporary relief for the peso. "Given the high volume of activity in the dollar-peso market, around $135 billion per day, the measures announced shouldn't have a significant impact on the exchange rate. The goal of the auctions is preventive," said \uc2 BBVA\uc2  analysts.\par \par \uc2 The IPC index of leading issues closed up 0.8% at 44752 points on volume of 280 million shares worth 8.6 billion pesos ($538 million).\par \par \uc2 Bellwether \uc2 America Movil\uc2  gained 2.7% to 15.67 pesos, while Mexican corn miller and tortilla maker Gruma closed up 1.5% to 211.11 pesos.\par \par \uc2 Among a handful of winners, Mexico's industrial conglomerate Alfa fell 0.2% to 32.02 pesos.\par \par \uc2 Write to Juan Montes at juan.montes@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 July 31, 2015 16:35 ET (20:35 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150731eb7v003o3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
