\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Mexico inflation hits record low in May, rate hike still eyed\b0\par\par\uc2 470 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juni 2015\par 20:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds comments from central banker, finance minister)\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY, June 9 (Reuters) - Mexico's annual inflation rate eased in May to a record low, pushed lower by summer electricity subsidies and contained by a sluggish economy, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still expected to raise interest rates when U.S. borrowing costs move higher.\par \par \uc2 Inflation in the 12 months through May slowed to 2.88 percent, the national statistics agency said on Tuesday, below the 2.92 percent expected in a Reuters poll, and the 3.06 percent annual rate in April.\par \par \uc2 The annual rate was the lowest on record according to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data going back to 1970.\par \par \uc2 Speaking after the data release, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board member Manuel Ramos Francia told a financial conference that inflation would remain tame in Latin America's second-biggest economy next year.\par \par \uc2 Last week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held its key interest rate at a record low of 3 percent, and said inflation would be below its 3 percent target for the rest of the year amid a sluggish economy.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said the data showed there was no sign of wider price pressures from a sharp slump in the peso \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , underpinning bets that \uc2 Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will wait to hike rates until after the Fed moves.\par \par \uc2 The peso hit a record low last week after strong U.S. jobs data backed expectations that the U.S. Federal Reserve will begin raising interest rates later this year and prompt investors to dump risky emerging market assets.\par \par \uc2 Mexican Finance Minister Luis Videgaray said on Tuesday at the same event that Mexico was well positioned to withstand the shock of higher U.S. rates given that it's economy is growing faster than other emerging-market peers and has relatively low debt levels.\par \par \uc2 He said that authorities were prepared to use the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reserves, more than $190 billion, to ensure an orderly \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the peso market.\par \par \uc2 "We have sufficient liquidity to guarantee the ordered working of the exchange market, even in moments of high volatility that could result above all from the adjustment of U.S. monetary policy," Videgaray said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  avoids directly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, but the country's exchange commission has activated two different dollar auction programs to suport the peso.\par \par \uc2 Tuesday's data showed consumer prices fell 0.50 percent in May from April on lower electricity costs as well as lower egg and tomato prices.\par \par \uc2 Core inflation, which strips out some volatile food and energy costs, rose 0.12 percent. Both were just below expectations in the Reuters poll. (Reporting by Michael O'Boyle and Noe Torres; Editing by W Simon and Alan Crosby) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-6-9T19:57:32.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150609eb6900dkc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
