\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Mexico officials extend dollar auction program to shield peso\b0\par\par\uc2 266 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Mai 2015\par 19:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, background on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  programs)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 MEXICO\b0 \highlight\uc2  CITY, May 22 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  commission said Friday it would extend a daily dollar auction program and could take additional measures to help shield the peso from global volatility.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso tumbled to a record low in March on a slump in oil prices and concerns that a possible U.S. interest rate hike, expected this year, may push investors to dump emerging market assets.\par \par \uc2 The commission, made up of officials from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the finance ministry, said in a statement it had decided to extend daily auctions of $52 million, which were set to expire on June 8, until at least Sept. 29. The auction, announced in March, has no minimum price.\par \par \uc2 The commission also said it will maintain a $200 million dollar auction announced in December that is triggered by losses of more than 1.5 percent.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  generally avoids the direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  used by other emerging markets, preferring more market-friendly mechanisms.\par \par \uc2 Analysts polled by Reuters this week said they doubted policymakers would resort to discretionary \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , expecting, rather, that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could increase the amount of dollars it sells or lower the threshold that would trigger the auction.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's weak peso has not yet fanned inflation, which reached a more than 9-year low in the first half of May, data showed on Friday. (Reporting by Michael O'Boyle and Alexandra Alper; Editing by Bernadette Baum) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-5-22T18:47:17.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150522eb5m00p03\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
