\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Mexico \highlight\uc2 's Stocks End Higher; Peso Gains as  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Harrup   \par \uc2 438 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2015\par 22:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 MEXICO\b0 \highlight\uc2  CITY--Mexican stocks closed higher Wednesday and the peso recovered ground as the \uc2 Bank of Mexico\uc2  took additional measures to shore up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after it had hit an all-time low against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 IPC\uc2  index of 35 most-traded stocks rose 0.6%, to 43,227 points, on volume of 230.5 million shares worth 7.71 billion pesos ($497 million).\par \par \uc2 The peso was quoted as closing in Mexico City at MXN15.5050 to the U.S. dollar, compared with MXN15.61 the previous session. The rate moved as low as MXN15.4050 intraday.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bank of Mexico\uc2  sold $52 million in the first of new daily dollar auctions that seek to support the peso by supplying dollars to the market from foreign reserves. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will offer that amount of dollars each day for at least the next three months.\par \par \uc2 To make dollars available for the sales, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will slow its accumulation of foreign reserves. Mexico's reserves, which are boosted by dollar inflows from crude oil sales by state energy company \uc2 Petroleos Mexicanos\uc2 , stood at $195 billion last week.\par \par \uc2 The auctions for $52 million are in addition to the $200 million that the bank offers on days when the peso weakens 1.5% from the previous session. The conditional auctions for $200 million have only been triggered twice since the mechanism was activated in December, although the peso has sunk to record lows against the dollar on prospects of higher U.S. interest rates and the drop in oil prices.\par \par \uc2 "The announcement confirms our view that the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  commission is less comfortable with the most recent depreciation of the peso as \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  dynamics do not reflect Mexico's fundamentals," Banorte said in a report.\par \par \uc2 Among individual stocks, shares of retailer \uc2 Wal-Mart de Mexico\uc2  SAB (WMMVY, WALMEX.MX) rose 0.6%, to MXN38.33.\par \par \uc2 Broadcast and media company \uc2 Grupo Televisa\uc2  SAB's (TV, TLEVISA.MX) CPO shares closed up 0.5%, at MXN106.56, while broadcaster TV Azteca SAB (AZTECA.MX) shares fell 1.7%, to MXN5.79.\par \par \uc2 The country's telecommunications regulator IFT opened bids for two new digital broadcast networks to complete with the incumbents, and was expected to award the concessions later Wednesday. Shares of \uc2 Grupo Radio Centro\uc2  SAB (RCENTRO.MX), which was one of the two bidders, closed up 1.7%, at MXN18.00, on low volume.\par \par \uc2 Write to Anthony Harrup at anthony.harrup@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 March 11, 2015 17:03 ET (21:03 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150311eb3b003yv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
