\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Mexico \highlight\uc2  peso slides, hits 6-year low despite  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 424 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2015\par 20:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (New throughout, adds bets on rate hike, adds market reaction, analyst comment)\par \par \uc2 By Luis Rojas\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY, March 6 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso tumbled on Friday despite \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , hitting a six-year low as investors fled emerging markets and fixed-income investors bet that higher interest rates are in store on both sides of the border.\par \par \uc2 Unexpectedly strong U.S. jobs data fueled bets that the U.S. Federal Reserve could raise interest rates in June, which could hasten the investor exodus from emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 Mexican policymakers have suggested they could raise local interest rates to increase the appeal of domestic debt.\par \par \uc2 "With the weak peso and the higher probability that Fed goes in June, that all means that we should think of a preemptive hike by Mexico," said Benito Berber, an analyst at Nomura in New York.\par \par \uc2 The peso slid more than 2 percent on Friday to 15.5210 per dollar, its weakest since March 2009. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold all $200 million offered in a rules-based auction to support the peso, which continued to fall.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's central bankers are worried that deep peso losses could affect financial stability.\par \par \uc2 Foreign investors have amassed record holdings of around 2.15 trillion pesos ($139 billion) of local-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt and a stampede for the doors by investors could drive much deeper peso losses, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 "Mexico is one of the markets with the heaviest foreign ownership," wrote analysts at Citi \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a note on Friday, saying the peso could soon hit 16 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Yields on short-term Mexican interest rate swaps jumped to the highest in more than a year as investors bet that Mexico could hike its benchmark interest rate from a record low of 3 percent by April.\par \par \uc2 Speaking at an event in Mexico City, \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Deputy Governor \uc2 Manuel Sanchez\uc2  said the peso slump had so far done little to fan inflation.\par \par \uc2 "There could be some contamination of inflation from the weakness of the peso; so far the contamination has been minimal, but it's a risk we're monitoring," he told reporters.\par \par \uc2 Sluggish domestic demand is expected to help contain price pressures in Latin America's second biggest economy in the months ahead, and Sanchez said he expected inflation to be around 3 percent both this year and next. ($1 = 15.4680 Mexican pesos) (Additional reporting by Michael O'Boyle; Editing by Simon Gardner and David Gregorio) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-3-6T20:21:32.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150306eb3600icx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
