\par\par \b \uc2 Bank of Mexico Sells Dollars to Stem Peso Rout\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Harrup   \par \uc2 524 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Dezember 2014\par 23:14\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY--The \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $200 million in an auction Thursday, its first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange market in 2 1/2 years as strong U.S. economic data and the continued slide in oil prices sent the peso to its weakest level since the 2009 crisis.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  placed the $200 million at an average price of 14.7544 pesos to the dollar. The bank received bids for $251 million.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  commission, run by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Finance Ministry, on Tuesday activated the auctions system, offering $200 million a day at a minimum price that is 1.5% above the previous day's fix. The fix is set by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  based on spot market rates.\par \par \uc2 The dollar auctions, which have been used in the past in times of financial market volatility, were in place from November 2011 to April 2013, and the last time the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars was in July 2012.\par \par \uc2 The peso was quoted in Mexico City at 14.7910 to the dollar following the auction, according to Infosel, compared with 14.5440 at the close Wednesday. The peso is at its weakest level against the dollar since March 2009, at the height of the global financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 Concerns about the U.S. Federal Reserve raising interest rates were fueled by an above-estimate increase in U.S. November retail sales, and a drop in weekly jobless claims, both of which suggest strength in the U.S. economy. The continued drop in oil prices Thursday added pressure on the peso, a Mexico City \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader said. January crude futures fell 99 cents to $59.95 a barrel on the \uc2 New York Mercantile Exchange\uc2 , the lowest for a front-month contract in more than five years.\par \par \uc2 Crude oil accounts for less than 10% of Mexico's exports, although oil and related taxes make up a significant part of federal government revenue. Mexican export crude priced at $54.40 a barrel on Wednesday, according to state oil company \uc2 Petr\u243\'00\'F3leos Mexicanos\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bank of Mexico\uc2  auctions are aimed at supplying dollars when authorities consider the peso to be depreciating too quickly.\par \par \uc2 "The purpose of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is to prevent a disorderly adjustment. A disorderly adjustment can sometimes unleash destabilization forces that are difficult to control (e.g., capital flight, untamable inflation expectations)," Nomura said in a report.\par \par \uc2 Nomura's recommendation last week to sell dollars at 14.20 pesos on expectations that the weakening should reverse course hit a stop-loss this week as the exchange rate broke past 14.50, with a loss on the trade.\par \par \uc2 "We failed to recognize that, while the speed of the depreciation was unwarranted given Mexico's fundamentals, the MXN would continue to sell off, responding more to factors such as real money rushing to hedge \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk and other market players using USDMXN as way to short emerging markets," Nomura said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Anthony Harrup at anthony.harrup@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 December 11, 2014 17:14 ET (22:14 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141211eacb00472\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
