\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Mexico \highlight\uc2  Finance Min Videgaray: No Need to  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  on Peso -Bloomberg\b0\par\par\uc2 187 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Januar 2014\par 17:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Mexican Finance Minister Luis Videgaray said Friday there's no need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the peso, which fell to an 18-month low earlier in the day, as there is sufficient liquidity in the Mexican peso market.\par \par \uc2 "The Mexican peso market is, fortunately, highly liquid and at the moment doesn't require any support," Mr. Videgaray told Bloomberg News from Davos, Switzerland. "We have a very liquid market and we don't see the need to inject liquidity, to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 Mr. Videgaray said the peso's weakening is in line with other emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Exchange Commission last April suspended a mechanism where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would auction $400 million on days when the peso was 2% weaker from the previous day. Last time the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars was July 2012.\par \par \uc2 Full story at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.bloomberg.com/news/2014-01-24/videgaray-says-no-need-to-intervene-as-mexico-s-peso-weakens.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.bloomberg.com/news/2014-01-24/videgaray-says-no-need-to-\b  \highlight22intervene\b0 \highlight22 -as-\b  \highlight22mexico\b0 \highlight22 -s-peso-weakens.html}}}\par \par \uc2 Write to nymonitoring@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 January 24, 2014 11:18 ET (16:18 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140124ea1o00277\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw1