\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil real rallies as  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  program extended\b0\par\par\uc2 394 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Dezember 2013\par 20:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO, Dec 5 (Reuters) - Brazil's real jumped more than one percent on Thursday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would extend its \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program into 2014, while \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso edged down before a congressional debate over a much-anticipated energy reform. Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose in general even as strong U.S. gross domestic product and jobs data fueled expectations that the U.S. Federal Reserve may soon start winding down its stimulus program. * The Brazilian real rose 1.1 percent after four consecutive sessions of losses, boosted by remarks from \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief \uc2 Alexandre Tombini\uc2 , who announced that the bank's daily \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program will be extended into 2014 "with some adjustments." * \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  currently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market through the sale of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps, derivatives that provide investors with protection against a possible depreciation of the real.\par \par \uc2  It also sells dollars on the spot market through repurchase agreements. * When announcing the extension of Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, Tombini said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  aims at curbing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility that could limit the impact of monetary policy over inflation. * Brazil's short-dated interest-rate futures ended slightly higher as investors considered that minutes of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's latest monetary policy meeting did not make it clear that policymakers will slow down the pace of monetary tightening in January, as some analysts expected. * Longer-date interest-rate futures fell sharply, however, as the real's rally reduced concern about the impact of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on inflation. * Mexico's peso edged 0.1 percent lower after a top ruling party senator said a key energy reform bill would be presented at a committee meeting on Friday rather than Thursday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1930 GMT:\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                             Daily  YTD pct\par                                          pct   change\par                              Latest   change  \par  Brazil real                 2.3588     1.22   -13.52\par                                               \par  Mexico peso                13.0570    -0.11    -1.48\par                                               \par  Chile peso                529.8000     0.66    -9.65\par                                               \par  Colombia peso           1,940.0000     0.47    -8.97\par                                               \par  Peru sol                    2.8020     0.04    -8.96\par                                               \par  Argentina peso              6.2250    -0.40   -21.08\par  (interbank)                                  \par                                               \par  Argentina peso              9.6400    -0.21   -29.67\par  (parallel)                                   \par                                               \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Walter Brandimarte and Bruno Federowski; Editing by Diane Craft)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  | ABN | D | M | RBN | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020131208e9c500096\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
