\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Mexico peso firms on Carstens remark; real gains\b0\par\par\uc2 504 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 April 2013\par 22:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Mexico peso gains 0.3 pct as Carstens says \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  undervalued\par \par \uc2 * Brazilian real up 0.2 pct on expected dollar inflows\par \par \uc2 * Chilean peso slides 0.2 pct as copper prices slump\par \par \uc2 By Jean Arce\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, April 26 (Reuters) - The Mexican peso gained on Friday after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief \uc2 Agustin Carstens\uc2  said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was undervalued, suggesting policymakers would tolerate a stronger exchange rate before \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market.\par \par \uc2 Other Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  suffered as weaker-than-expected U.S. GDP growth data reduced investors' appetite for commodities and emerging market assets, although the Brazilian real was boosted by expectations of dollar inflows from companies raising money from foreign investors.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso gained 0.3 percent to 12.1490 per dollar as Carstens said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was still undervalued compared to before the 2008 crisis, and that optimism about economic reforms could fuel even more gains.\par \par \uc2 "That gives me an indication that he will remain comfortable if the peso continues on its appreciation trend toward 12 per dollar or stronger," said Enrique Alvarez, head of Latin America research at IDEAglobal in New York.\par \par \uc2 The peso hit a 20-month high of 12.04 per dollar just 15 days ago, but gave up some of its gains in the past few sessions amid signs of an economic slowdown in the United States, Mexico's main trading partner.\par \par \uc2 "What Carstens is saying is that he isn't going to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the peso hits 12.00 per dollar," said Alfredo Puig, a trader with Vector brokerage in Monterrey, \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The market is now thinking \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could come if the peso hits 11.70 to the dollar, he added.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real firmed for the third consecutive session as investors anticipated dollar inflows from the initial public offerings of \uc2 Banco do Brasil\uc2 's insurance unit \uc2 BB Seguridade\uc2  and Gol airline's frequent-flyer program Smiles.\par \par \uc2 BB Seguridade\uc2  raised about $5.7 billion on Thursday, the world's largest IPO in seven months, while Smiles obtained some $560 million. Both attracted a great number of foreign investors.\par \par \uc2 Other Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  posted losses, however, as a disappointing economic performance by the United States in the first quarter weighed on prices of commodities and other risky assets.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso slid 0.25 percent as the price of copper, the country's main export product, dropped more than 2 percent.\par \par \uc2 Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  prices at 2000 GMT:\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                          daily %    YTD %\par                                   change   change\par                          Latest           \par Brazil real                1.9980     0.18     2.10\par                                           \par Mexico peso               12.1490     0.26     5.89\par                                           \par Chile peso               472.9000    -0.25     1.23\par                                           \par Colombia peso           1834.2000    -0.19    -3.72\par                                           \par Peru sol                 