\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Mexico peso rallies to 19-month high, Brazil real flat\b0\par\par\uc2 505 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 April 2013\par 23:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Optimism about upcoming U.S. jobs data encourages risk taking\par \par \uc2 * Investors alert for possible Brazil cenbank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  peso jumps 0.8 pct; Brazil real unchanged\par \par \uc2 By Michael O'Boyle and Bruno Federowski\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY/SAO PAULO, April 2 (Reuters) - The Mexican peso hit a 19-month high on Tuesday as a rally on Wall Street encouraged investors to take on riskier emerging market assets, but the Brazilian real ended nearly unchanged for the second consecutive session on fears of a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso jumped 0.8 percent to 12.2720 per dollar, its strongest level since early September 2011, as major U.S. stock indexes rose to record levels.\par \par \uc2 Investors were growing optimistic that key U.S. jobs data on Friday will show the U.S. economy is on solid footing, increasing prospects for Mexican exports. The United States is Mexico's main trading partner.\par \par \uc2 "The peso could reach 12.15 per dollar with a good U.S. jobs data on Friday, but people should start buying dollars then," said Mario Copca, an analyst with CI brokerage in Mexico City.\par \par \uc2 The peso has rallied more than 6 percent from a December low, helped by bets the new government will push through major economic reforms.\par \par \uc2 But the surge may be petering out. Technical momentum indicators show the peso in "overbought" territory, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's moving-average convergence divergence (MACD) indicator was on the verge of flashing a "sell" sign.\par \par \uc2 In Brazil, the real ended practically unchanged at 2.0201 per dollar, with investors wary of a possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Many analysts believe the \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants the real to remain within a tight range of 1.95 reais to around 2 reais per dollar - slightly stronger than it was at the end of 2012 - to avoid inflation passthrough.\par \par \uc2 "There is no reason for bigger changes in the exchange rate. If you are going to test the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, you want to do it carefully or as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can suddenly dump dollars on the market," said Mario Battistel, a manager at Fair brokerage in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 Brazilian policymakers last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market last Wednesday, when the real neared the level of 2.03 per dollar. On Tuesday, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president \uc2 Alexandre Tombini\uc2  reiterated that the bank is always ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to make sure the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is working properly.\par \par \uc2 Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  prices at 2125 GMT:\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                            Daily  YTD pct\par                                      pct   change\par                          Latest   change  \par Brazil real                2.0203     0.01     0.98\par                                           \par Mexico peso               12.2720     0.76     4.83\par                                           \par Chile peso               472.0000     0.11     1.42\par                                           \par Colombia peso           1814.0400     0.44    -2.65\par                              