\par\par \b \uc2 INTERVIEW-Mexico has learned to stick with flexible peso-Aportela\b0\par\par\uc2 501 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2013\par 20:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Authorities have not discussed reactivating dollar put auctions\par \par \uc2  * No other \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures have been discussed \par \par \uc2  By Michael O'Boyle\par \par \uc2  PANAMA CITY, March 16 (Reuters) - Mexico is committed to maintaining its freely floating exchange rate and is not currently contemplating any new mechanism to slow strong gains in the peso, deputy finance minister Fernando Aportela said on Saturday.\par \par \uc2  The peso hit a 18-month high against the dollar last week, boosted by growing confidence in a reform drive by the new government and potential credit-rating upgrades, sparking speculation that authorities could take measures to slow the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's advance.\par \par \uc2  Aportela said Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  commission, made up of members of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the finance ministry, had not discussed any new measures to try and slow the peso's advance.\par \par \uc2  "Mexico has learned that the sound macroeconomic policy of having a well-administered flexible exchange rate pays off in the end," Aportela told Reuters at an \uc2 Inter-American Development Bank\uc2  meeting in Panama City. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  has eschewed the direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and capital controls that other emerging-market countries have deployed in recent years to tame local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains resulting from a flood of liquidity from developed markets seeking higher returns.\par \par \uc2  Investors are watching to see if Mexico will reinstate a more market-friendly mechanism of auctioning dollar "put" options, which could indicate authorities are growing uncomfortable with the pace of peso gains. \par \par \uc2  The options, which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  used to accumulate reserves and slow peso gains in 2010 and 2011, give investors the right to sell dollars to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a better rate than the spot rate when the cost of dollars in pesos falls below its 20-day moving average.\par \par \uc2  Aportela said policymakers had not discussed reinstating the auctions and they were not looking at any other tools either. "The set of instruments we have are what they are," he said. \par \par \uc2  Mexico's peso, one of the world's most liquid emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has oscillated wildly since the financial crisis, tracking the ups and downs of riskier global assets.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has yet to recover to the levels seen before  late 2008, which has helped boost the competitiveness of Mexican exports amid sluggish global growth.\par \par \uc2  "The exchange rate has shown itself to be effective in absorbing this type of external volatility," Aportela said.\par \par \uc2  Market players read a 50 basis point cut to Mexico's benchmark rate to a record low of 4 percent on March 8 as a bid by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to try and curb the appeal of local-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed-income assets to speculators.\par \par \uc2  The \uc2 Banco de Mexico\uc2  warned that heavy inflows could lead to an 'unnecessary' tightening in monetary conditions. A stronger peso could create drag on growth by crimping exporters' profits. \par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Luis Rojas; Editing by David Brunnstrom)\par \par \uc2 MEXICO-ECONOMY/ | C | D | E | M | O | U | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | ABN | RBN | NAT | ABX | BNX | FUN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130319e93g0013k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
