\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  to keep governments under pressure\b0\par\par\uc2 654 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Februar 2013\par 16:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * For poll data see\par \par \uc2 * Colombia, Peru, \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to extend gains\par \par \uc2 * Chile peso seen weakening, but \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  not ruled out\par \par \uc2 * Brazil to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in tight range\par \par \uc2 By Silvio Cascione\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Feb 6 (Reuters) - Latin American governments will probably have a tough time trying to curb \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains this year as improving market conditions boost dollar inflows, a Reuters poll showed.\par \par \uc2 After failing to foresee a surge in many Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past few months, economists and strategists revised their forecasts to predict another leg of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation in Mexico, Peru and Colombia.\par \par \uc2 Such an outlook means that investors should remain wary for further government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - not only in those countries but also in Brazil, the birthplace of the latest "\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  wars", and in Chile, where prospects of a weaker peso did not eliminate chances of increased dollar purchases.\par \par \uc2 "There's a good chance that in the current 'risk on' environment the Chilean peso will continue to appreciate towards 460 per dollar," said Michael Henderson, an economist with Capital Economics. "We think if it approaches 460 that might provoke the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  into announcing measures such as \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases to weaken the peso."\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso should remain at the current 472 per dollar this month, weakening to 480.00 in six months and to 486.59 in 12 months on prospects of feeble copper prices, according to the median of 13 forecasts.\par \par \uc2 Dollar purchases - the classic government tool - have already been used in Colombia, with little success so far. After increasing the daily amount of dollars purchased to $30 million from $20 million, Finance Minister \uc2 Mauricio Cardenas\uc2  said the government is planning to take on less external debt.\par \par \uc2 Six out of seven analysts who replied to an extra question on the Reuters poll said they expect additional government measures to curb the Colombian peso's gains in the next six months. The most cited was the extension of the dollar purchase program from May to the end of the year.\par \par \uc2 Even so, the Colombian peso is seen gaining ground to 1,780 per dollar in one month, 1,772.50 in six months and 1,770 in 12 months, according to the median of 14 forecasts. It last traded at 1,790.10 per dollar on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Peru has been more aggressive than Chile and Colombia in protecting its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Not only has it bought dollars, the government also announced it would prepay up to $1.5 billion in debt this year and flirted with capital controls by tightening reserve requirements on bank accounts denominated in dollars.\par \par \uc2 Analysts still expect Peru's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the nuevo sol , to strengthen this year, though.\par \par \uc2 It should trade at 2.560 per dollar in one month, 2.530 per dollar in six months and 2.520 per dollar in twelve months. It was at 2.5775 on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 All the five top Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  gained between about 1.5 and 7 percent since mid-November. In the latest Reuters poll, in October, analysts said that \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  had little room to strengthen as government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was expected to yield better results.\par \par \uc2 The strongest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far has been seen in Brazil, where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been keeping its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real, trading within a narrow band between 1.98 and 2.05 per dollar through dollar purchases and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap auctions.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the country less likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. However, a rate cut could help stem further gains in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts said.\par \par \uc2 (For other poll stories, see )\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Noe Torres, Jean Luis Arce and Michael O'Boyle in Mexico City, Nelson Bocanegra in Bogota, Ursula Scollo in Lima and Anthony Esposito and Moises Avila in Santiago; Editing by)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /LATAM-POLL | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | NAT | U | C | O | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130209e92600073\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
