\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazilian real gains after  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  acts\b0\par\par\uc2 586 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Dezember 2012\par 00:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Brazil's real up 1.39 pct after auction, swap offers\par \par \uc2  * Mexico's peso edges lower, on fiscal cliff concerns \par \par \uc2 (Updates prices, adds context)\par \par \uc2  By Asher Levine and Alexandra Alper\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO/MEXICO CITY, Dec 26 (Reuters) - The Brazilian real strengthened on Wednesday following heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, while \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso was little changed as worries over U.S. budget talks weighed.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  three times in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Wednesday in an effort to limit recent weakness in the real, which has dropped nearly 9.0 percent against the U.S. dollar this year. \par \par \uc2  Early on Wednesday, the bank conducted an auction to sell up to $2 billion on the spot market with repurchase agreements, which aims to provide liquidity to the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market at year-end.\par \par \uc2  The move was followed by two \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap auctions, both offering 40,000 contracts with a maturity of Feb. 1, 2013. The bank sold a combined total of 37,000 contracts, which are derivatives that emulate the selling of dollars in the futures markets.\par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants the dollar around 2.05 reais, considering the market was very calm and there was no reason for it to step in," said Reginaldo Siaca, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Advanced Corretora in Sao Paulo. "With the auctions, it is signaling the band it is comfortable with for the end of the year."\par \par \uc2  The real strengthened sharply after the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , gaining 1.39 percent to close at 2.05 per U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had last carried out a swap auction on Dec. 3, when the real closed at 2.119 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  saw that a dollar close to 2.10 reais would be harmful for inflation," said Jo\u227\'00\'E3o Medeiros, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Pioneer Corretora in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2  The Mexican peso edged down 0.21 percent to 13.0120 per dollar as anxieties remained over unresolved austerity issues facing the United States, Mexico's biggest trading partner. \par \par \uc2  "Mexico is really the barometer for the reality of the market over the holidays, which is thin (trading) and growing concerns over the fiscal cliff," said RBS economist Flavia Cattan-Naslausky. \par \par \uc2  She pointed to U.S. President \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 's decision to return early to Washington from vacation to tackle the looming package of tax hikes and spending cuts, along with an upcoming debt ceiling debate, as fueling investor concern. \par \par \uc2  The \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  on Wednesday announced the first of a series of measures that should push back the day when the government will exceed its legal borrowing authority as imposed by Congress by around two months. \par \par \uc2  Without any action, Treasury said the government is set to reach its $16.4 trillion debt ceiling on Dec. 31. \par \par \uc2  Still, the Mexican peso has performed well this year, firming more than 7.0 percent since 2011, and Cattan-Naslausky warned against reading too much into market moves during periods of light trading.\par \par \uc2  Chile's peso edged up 0.08 percent to 479.10 per U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  raised Chile's sovereign credit rating a notch on Wednesday to AA-minus from A-plus, citing the export-dependent economy's resilience to fallout from the global slowdown.  \par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Danielle Fonseca and Anthony Esposito; Editing by \uc2 Leslie Adler\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020121229e8cq0007f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
