\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Funds Back in the Black in 2012 - but Only Just\b0\par\par\uc2 680 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 November 2012\par 16:15\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -- \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds gain 0.14% on average in the 10 months to October\par \par \uc2 -- Timing investor swings has been key to performing well in 2012\par \par \uc2 -- \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  easing has made it harder to make money in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 By Clare Connaghan\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds have barely made a profit in 2012 because the euro-zone crisis and policies of the world's central banks have made it harder for traders to make money investing in the $4 trillion-a-day \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 But at least they are doing better than in 2011.\par \par \uc2 After losing more than 6% on average last year, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 -focused investment managers on average made a gain of 0.14% in the 10 months to October, according to Parker Global Strategies, a U.S.-based company that tracks the performance of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds globally.\par \par \uc2 That compares with a 2% gain over the same period for all hedge funds, across all financial markets, according to the \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  Core Hedge Fund Index.\par \par \uc2 "It's been a frustrating year again--there haven't been any big macro trends out there," said Paul Lambert, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Insight Investment in London.\par \par \uc2 Policy easing by central banks globally, from the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  and \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 , have helped to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in check by neutralizing the risk of a breakup of the euro zone and squashing interest rate differentials. Along with the efforts made by several emerging market governments, such as Brazil's, to stop their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciating, that has made it harder for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  investors to make money.\par \par \uc2 "There has been a slight improvement this year in the performance of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds but it's still been quite a difficult year," said Pablo Frei, head of multi-manager programs at Zurich-based funds firm Quaesta Capital.\par \par \uc2 A key part of the problem is the way in which financial markets have tended to behave, switching between periods of so-called risk-on and risk-off as investors have indiscriminately blown hot or cold in response to the euro-zone crisis.\par \par \uc2 For \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, that has meant piling into \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  perceived as safe havens, such as the dollar and yen, when confidence is low while selling emerging-market and commodity-linked \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  perceived as risky. And whenever investors have grown upbeat, those flows have reversed. As a result, more traditional and discriminate market drivers such as a country's relative economic fundamentals have taken a back seat.\par \par \uc2 "You haven't really had a trending market this year so unless you've been able to time the risk-on/risk-off moves correctly then you would have struggled," said Michael DePalma, chief investment officer of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategies at AllianceBernstein in New York.\par \par \uc2 Compared with equities, where the investor can pick between different industrial sectors or even individual stocks, there are fewer choices when it comes to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  investing. As a result, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  investors have been scrambling over an even smaller number of trades.\par \par \uc2 "The fact is there haven't been a huge number of very good ideas this year, so the money that's found its way into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market has crowded itself into a couple of places like the Mexican peso," said Mr. DePalma.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso, which has gained more than 5% this year against the dollar, has been a big favorite of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  investors, who have been encouraged by Mexico's relatively strong fundamentals. The economy is expected by the government to grow 3.5% this year. The \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also been of the non-\b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist\b0 \highlight\uc2  kind.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  managers that specialize in higher-yielding emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such as the Mexican peso, are having a better year than most, said Diane Miller, a principal at U.K. consulting firm Mercer.\par \par \uc2 But overall 2012 has been another difficult year for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds, which last delivered returns of more than 1% in 2008.\par \par \uc2 Write to Clare Connaghan at clare.connaghan@dowjones.com [ 14-11-12 1515GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020121114e8be000ww\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
