\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Mexico peso steady on rate warning, real flat\b0\par\par\uc2 557 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Oktober 2012\par 17:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  warns could raise interest rates soon\par \par \uc2 * Traders fear additional \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Brazil\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  peso steady near 13/dlr, Brazil real flat\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Colombia \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  holds rates steady\par \par \uc2 (Adds detail, comments, \uc2 Colombia \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decision)\par \par \uc2 By Walter Brandimarte and Lorena Segura\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO/MEXICO CITY, Oct 26 (Reuters) - The Mexican peso steadied on Friday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  warned it could raise interest rates soon, potentially increasing the allure of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while trading in the Brazilian real slowed to a near halt on fears of additional government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Colombian peso weakened before a key \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decision on monetary policy, with some traders betting the bank could lower interest rates, making the peso less attractive.\par \par \uc2 After markets closed, however, the bank kept rates unchanged at 4.75 percent.\par \par \uc2 Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were little changed in general after better-than-expected U.S. GDP data for the third quarter offset concerns about weak corporate earnings.\par \par \uc2 Lackluster corporate earnings in the United States, including those of \uc2 Apple Inc\uc2  and \uc2 Amazon.com Inc\uc2  , added to economic concerns and drove investors to the perceived safety of the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Sentiment improved slightly after data showed the U.S. economy grew a little more than expected in the third quarter, but not enough to hold U.S. stocks in positive territory.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso weakened 0.17 percent to 480.30 per dollar, erasing part of Thursday's gains.\par \par \uc2 "The peso is weakening as earnings from major global companies came in worse than expected. That is hurting commodities prices and stocks," said Eugenio Cortes, head of forward markets at EuroAmerica in Santiago.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso erased early losses to trade at 12.9899 per dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  surprised economists by warning it could soon tighten monetary policy if price pressures do not start to abate.\par \par \uc2 "This can be a reading of more confidence, that (the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) won't allow, under any circumstance, pressure on rates," said Mario Copca, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at CI brokerage in Mexico.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also said a recent rise in the value of the peso has helped limit price pressures, in another sign that policymakers will not fight \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains.\par \par \uc2 In Brazil, however, expectations of continued government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  have drastically reduced volumes and volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 The real was little changed, closing at 2.0258 per dollar\par \par \uc2 as investors anticipated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may sell more reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps next week to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the current level, which government officials consider beneficial to exporters.\par \par \uc2 Brazil \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice this week with the sale of those swaps, or derivatives contracts that emulate the purchase of dollars in the futures market.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                        daily %  year-to\par                                 change   date %\par                        Latest            change\par Brazil real              2.0258    -0.08    -7.76\par                                         \par Mexico peso             12.9899     0.17     7.51\par                                         \par Argentina peso*          6.3600     0.16   -25.63\par                                         \par Chile peso             480.3000    -0.17     8.12\par                                         \par Colombia peso        1,828.0000    -0.54     6.04\par                                         \par Peru sol                 2.5980    -0.35     3.81\par                                         \par * Argentine peso's rate between                  \par brokerages                                \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Additional reporting by Moises Avila in Santiago; Editing by Andrea Ricci and Lisa Shumaker)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | NAT | Z | C | O | U | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020121029e8aq0014m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
